course: dictionary
lesson: 8903
title: Shun and keeping away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To shun someone is to keep away from them on purpose and refuse to talk to them. To shun something is to avoid it on purpose. Shun is a verb, so its forms are shun, shuns, shunned and shunning. «She shuns the spotlight» means she avoids being the centre of attention.
explain: Shun is a strong word. When a village shuns a family for being different, the family is left out and made to feel alone, which is a kind of bullying. Look for the clues: keeping away on purpose, refusing to talk, leaving someone out.
explain: Shun is not the same as forgetting or not noticing. You shun something because you choose to keep away from it. Try the swap test: if you can put "avoid" into the sentence and it still makes sense, you are probably reading shun correctly.
fact: Shun means to keep away from someone or something on purpose.
fact: «The village shunned the new family for being different.» means the village refused to talk to them.
fact: «She shuns the spotlight» means she avoids being the centre of attention.
fact: Useful phrases: «shunned by», «shun publicity», «shun the limelight».
fact: Being shunned hurts. Including others is the opposite of shunning them.
exercise: «The villagers shunned the stranger and would not speak to her.» What does shunned mean? | Invited to the party | Given a present | *Kept away from on purpose | Sang a song for
exercise: «Rena shuns the limelight at school.» What does shuns mean here? | Copies | *Avoids | Wants | Enjoys
exercise: Yesterday the class ___ Tom at lunch and sat somewhere else. Which word fits the gap? | shun | *shunned | shunning | shuns
test: «Ben shuns publicity and never gives interviews.» What does shuns publicity mean? | *Avoids attention from the media | Waves at every camera | Loves being photographed | Sends out press releases every week
test: Why is being shunned hurtful? | It means being given a prize | *It means being left out and refused talk | It makes you taller | It means being asked to lead the team
exam: Which sentence shows someone avoiding the spotlight on purpose? | They invite the press to every match | She waves to every camera in the room | He sings loudly on stage every week | *He shuns the spotlight and stays at the back
